This error is actually progress: your route found the account and reached the update step. The problem is now your $set: req.body.

The error:

Performing an update on the path '_id' would modify the immutable field '_id'

means your Postman body contains an _id field.

MongoDB automatically creates _id for every document, and it cannot be changed. If you send:

{
  "_id": "65abc123...",
  "firstName": "Mike"
}

then this:

{ $set: req.body }

becomes:

{
  $set: {
    _id: "65abc123...",
    firstName: "Mike"
  }
}

MongoDB rejects it.

Fix 1 (recommended): only update the fields you allow

For a first name update:

const { firstName } = req.body;

const result = await collection.updateOne(
	{ email: req.query.email },
	{ $set: { firstName } }
);

Now _id can never accidentally be changed.

Fix 2: remove _id before updating

If you want to update multiple fields:

const updateData = { ...req.body };
delete updateData._id;

const result = await collection.updateOne(
	{ email: req.query.email },
	{ $set: updateData }
);
